:: OC Kazu The Eye 3 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<span style="Color: Yellow">Your brain takes a second to process everything as your heart rate finally slows down and you finally breathe in. Your mind is a mix of anger at such a cruel joke and confusion about the reveal that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span>’s eye is fake.</span> You open your mouth to express one of these emotions, but only vague noises come out. Until you get out a single word asking about the eye. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s a prosthetic, had it…”</span> He thinks for a minute, tapping the eye. <span style="Color: Yellow">Despite it being glass, the sight does make your stomach turn a little,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“…a while. Can’t recall exacts. I lost my eye when I was little.”</span> He shrugs. You want to ask more questions but feel it may be too personal to ask and are already overcome with information overload. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“To be fair, you took it better than the last person I did that too.”</span> He laughs, smiling evilly, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Some highschooler prick wanted to pick a fight at the mall. But when I popped my eye out, the kid was so scared he screamed and then pissed himself! Right in front of his friends, it was glorious. So, as long as you’re all dry down there, you handled it pretty well.”</span> <br>
<br>
It is only as he laughs again, patting you on the back, that your nerves finally calm down. You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kazu</span> hang out for a bit around the playground, but you can’t get the image of his eye popping out of his head out of your mind. <span style="Color: Yellow">You’re pretty sure you’re going to have nightmares about that…</span> <br>
